& [SelectedPurpose] is one pure supplied ordered-inventory commitment
  + consume exactly one completed WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssembly by value
  + retain that complete non-deserializable assembly in one new output-only result
  + reapply current M2A validation to every exposed TopologyEntryObservation
  + verify assembly member count, entry count, and total regular-file byte count remain exactly correlated
  + encode every ordered observation under one explicit stable binary grammar
  + derive one lowercase SHA-256 digest by bounded streaming updates
  - never: accept raw observations, member vectors, carrier fragments, or caller-declared digest success
  - never: sort, normalize, repair, renumber, or reinterpret an observation
  - never: construct TopologyReceipt or claim physical inventory evidence

& [WhyThisSlice] is dependency ordered
  + the completed assembly supplies exactly one root-first, parent-closed, duplicate-free, bounded observation order
  + an aggregate inventory commitment is undefined until that structural subject and order are fixed
  + explicit canonical encoding prevents serializer, endianness, enum-layout, and concatenation ambiguity
  + TopologyReceipt already separates ordered_inventory_sha256 from policy_sha256 and admission_receipt_sha256
  + the inventory digest must therefore commit observation content and order without mixing in policy or proof-lineage syntax
  + physical producer, Git reconciliation, repeat-inventory equality, receipt issuance, and admission remain later boundaries

& [Input] is one completed assembly only
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedTopologyInventoryAssembly
  + input is consumed by value only after every pure check succeeds
  + ordered_members is read through its immutable getter
  + each member observation is read through topology_observation
  + complete root, directory, regular-file, stability, content-binding, preflight, projection, and assembly lineage remains nested in the retained input
  - never: derive Deserialize, Default, From raw observations, public fields, or a public success constructor for the input or output

& [Plan] is strict and bounded
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestPlan
  + [profile] exact cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + [commitment_identity] is a nonzero unsigned 64-bit caller correlation value
  + [encoding_profile] is exact cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + [encoded_plan_maximum_bytes] is 4096 before strict JSON decoding
  + unknown, missing, malformed, overlong, wrong-profile, and zero-identity values reject
  - never: include a supplied digest, entries, limits, deadline, physical claim, consistency class, receipt, or admission decision in the plan

& [DigestSubject] is exact
  + the domain separator is exact ASCII cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1 followed by one zero byte
  + one u64 entry count follows the domain separator
  + observations follow in the assembly's existing root-first structural order
  + every observation commits relative_path, kind, mode_class, attributes, identity volume_serial, identity file_id, number_of_links, streams, length, content_sha256, and observation_ordinal
  + every stream commits name, size, and kind in current validated stream order
  + the stream sequence count and every optional-field presence are committed
  - never: include assembly plan, limits, deadline, assembly identity, commitment identity, projection identity, entry-reference identity, carrier profiles, or lower proof-lineage records
  - never: describe exclusion of lineage as discarding it; the output wrapper retains the complete assembly separately from the digest subject

& [PrimitiveEncoding] is architecture independent
  + [u32] exactly four big-endian bytes
  + [u64] exactly eight big-endian bytes
  + [enum] exactly one specified nonzero byte tag and never a Rust discriminant or serializer label
  + [option] exactly one zero byte for absent or one byte for present followed by the value encoding
  + [text] u64 big-endian UTF-8 byte count followed by exact UTF-8 bytes
  + [hex_digest] validated lowercase 64-hex is decoded to exactly 32 raw bytes
  + [file_identity] validated lowercase 32-hex is decoded to exactly 16 raw bytes
  + [sequence] u64 big-endian element count followed by each element encoding
  + [field] one specified nonzero field tag precedes every field
  + [entry] one entry-start tag precedes one complete observation
  - never: use platform-native integer layout, usize, Debug, JSON, CBOR, serde field order, locale, Unicode normalization, or implicit delimiters

& [ClosedTags] are explicit source requirements
  + entry-start is 0x01
  + relative_path is 0x10, kind is 0x11, mode_class is 0x12, attributes is 0x13
  + volume_serial is 0x14, file_id is 0x15, number_of_links is 0x16, streams is 0x17
  + length is 0x18, content_sha256 is 0x19, observation_ordinal is 0x1A
  + root_directory, directory, and regular_file kind tags are 0x01, 0x02, and 0x03
  + directory, regular_non_executable, and regular_executable mode tags are 0x01, 0x02, and 0x03
  + unnamed_default and named_data stream-kind tags are 0x01 and 0x02
  + each stream begins with 0x20; its name, size, and kind field tags are 0x21, 0x22, and 0x23
  + all unlisted tags and alternate encodings reject at any future decoder boundary

& [EvaluationOrder] is fail closed
  + decode and validate the exact plan before consuming assembly success
  + require assembly profile remain exact
  + require ordered member length convert exactly to u64 and equal assembly entry_count
  + invoke current ValidateTopologyForm for each member observation
  + require root-first kind and path shape and require each observation ordinal equal its one-based sequence position
  + recompute regular-file length sum with checked arithmetic and require exact assembly total_file_bytes equality
  + initialize the bounded streaming SHA-256 accumulator
  + write exact domain, entry count, tags, framing, and field values in declared order
  + finalize one 32-byte digest and expose canonical lowercase 64-hex
  + release one output-only result retaining plan and complete assembly
  + first failure returns no digest success or partial output

& [StreamingBound] is constant-space with respect to inventory bytes
  + fixed-width values update the accumulator from stack arrays
  + strings update with their encoded u64 length and existing UTF-8 slice without copying the full inventory
  + validated hex values decode through fixed 16-byte or 32-byte arrays
  + no complete canonical byte vector or duplicate observation collection is allocated
  + existing assembly storage is retained rather than cloned for success
  + SHA-256 implementation may be reused or carefully extracted from the proven supplied-content-digest implementation only if SJS authorizes the exact source change
  + no new dependency or Cargo.lock change is required

& [Output] is a nonforgeable supplied commitment
  + [type] WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigest
  + private fields are profile, encoding_profile, plan, assembly, and ordered_inventory_sha256
  + derives Serialize but not Deserialize or Default
  + immutable getters expose the exact profile strings, plan, retained assembly, and digest
  + no public field, mutable getter, public success constructor, From, or Into exists
  - never: expose digest success apart from the retained assembly that formed its subject

& [DigestSemantics] are narrow
  + equal digest values under the same exact encoding profile mean equal encoded ordered observation sequences except for ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  + changing any committed field, stream fact, optional presence, sequence count, entry count, or member order changes the encoded subject
  + changing only policy, limits, deadline, correlation identities, carrier profiles, or lower lineage does not change the inventory digest subject
  + the output is a supplied structural commitment suitable only as a future input to separately authorized physical and receipt logic
  - never: equate a digest with physical origin, completeness, freshness, temporal equality, atomicity, Git agreement, or admission

& [Faults] are bounded and atomic
  + [codes] are json, profile, commitment_identity, encoding_profile, topology_form, assembly, count, ordinal, accounting, hex, arithmetic, resource, and internal
  + exact nested TopologyFormFault is present only for topology_form
  + field is at most 64 Unicode scalars and message is at most 256 Unicode scalars
  + no fault contains a partial digest, full observation, carrier, assembly, or lower record
  + no partial success is returned

& [EvidenceGrades] remain explicit
  + [supplied] lower observations and content bytes at their original boundaries
  + [carrier_projected] complete output-only entry carriers
  + [structurally_assembled] bounded ordered supplied set
  + [current_revalidated] M2A observation validity and assembly accounting at this boundary
  + [canonically_committed] exact supplied ordered observation bytes under the selected encoding profile
  + [physically_observed] absent
  + [enumerated_complete] absent
  + [temporally_repeated] absent
  + [quiescent_double_inventory] absent
  + [receipted] absent
  + [admitted] absent

& [EffectBoundary] is zero
  + deterministic in-memory validation, encoding, and hashing only
  + no unsafe, Windows API, filesystem, path resolution, process, environment, clock, randomness, network, persistence, database, model, or tool call
  + no enumeration, traversal, Git reconciliation, physical fixture, double inventory, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, test-execution effect, cleanup, or promotion
  + no new Cargo dependency or lockfile delta

& [Requirements] are proposed
  + [M2B-SOTID-001] strict bounded plan with exact commitment and encoding profiles
  + [M2B-SOTID-002] complete output-only assembly input only
  + [M2B-SOTID-003] current M2A revalidation for every ordered observation
  + [M2B-SOTID-004] exact assembly count, root-first, kind, path, and ordinal correlations
  + [M2B-SOTID-005] checked total regular-file byte accounting correlation
  + [M2B-SOTID-006] exact domain separator and entry-count commitment
  + [M2B-SOTID-007] fixed big-endian integer and explicit enum-tag encoding
  + [M2B-SOTID-008] explicit option, text, digest, identity, sequence, field, entry, and stream framing
  + [M2B-SOTID-009] every TopologyEntryObservation and TopologyStreamFact semantic field committed
  + [M2B-SOTID-010] policy, correlation, carrier-profile, and proof-lineage exclusion from digest subject
  + [M2B-SOTID-011] bounded streaming SHA-256 without whole-inventory encoding allocation
  + [M2B-SOTID-012] private Serialize-only output retaining complete assembly and digest
  + [M2B-SOTID-013] closed bounded fault vocabulary and atomic failure
  + [M2B-SOTID-014] zero effects, unsafe, platform calls, dependencies, and lockfile delta
  + [M2B-SOTID-015] focused vectors, static boundary, global regression, evidence, audit, rollback, and provenance proof

& [Verification] must be proportional and effect free
  + exact known vectors include empty-descendant root-only and mixed nested inventory cases
  + field, optional-presence, stream, member-order, and entry-count perturbations demonstrate subject sensitivity
  + policy and correlation-identity perturbations demonstrate intentional subject exclusion while retained lineage changes
  + manual reference bytes independently reproduce at least one expected digest
  + static test rejects Deserialize, public success fields, alternate hash dependency, unsafe, platform calls, filesystem calls, and effect surfaces
  + focused debug and overflow-checked release, workspace regression, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, audit, and recursive evidence must pass
  + physical tests and effect-bearing builders remain uninvoked

& [Rollback] is exact
  + remove only the future module, export, tests, evidence, and closure records authorized by the future SJS signature
  + retain this raw source, manifest, SJS products, faults, and proof as immutable history
  + rollback never activates a different encoding or receipt path

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  - stop before code until this exact source is processed through governing SJS
  - stop on any hidden default, serializer-dependent byte form, native endianness, unspecified tag, unbounded allocation, or digest-subject ambiguity
  - stop on any claim that supplied canonical commitment proves physical inventory, completeness, temporal stability, quiescent equality, receipt validity, or admission
  - stop on any effect, dependency growth, unsafe, platform call, or authority beyond this pure slice

& [Next] is governing SJS only
  + preserve source SHA-256 and byte count in a separate source manifest
  + delineate, explode, refine, constrain, reapply constraints, prune, seed growth, data-design, justify, plan, register, phase lock, and sign before implementation
  + no implementation authority exists in this raw source
